.TH "HEE\-DEPLOY" "1" "" "" "HEE Tools"
.SH NAME
hee\-deploy \- publish a directory of markdown + images as a resume blog
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
hee deploy blog [DIR] [\-oper SLUG] [\-to lab|prod] [\-dry\-run] [\-no\-pr] [\-resume PATH]
hee deploy store [DIR] [\-slug S] [\-to lab|prod] [\-url URL] [\-dry\-run] [\-list\-missing]
hee deploy worker [DIR] \-name WORKER [\-host HOSTNAME] [\-dry\-run]
hee deploy help | blog help | store help | worker help
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IP
.EX
post, or a store directory as the live store on the lab

  Turns a directory shaped like:

    mkdir my\-new\-blog && cd my\-new\-blog
    echo \[dq]# Title of new blog\[dq] > blog.md
    cp /some/path/images* .
    ls {a,b,c,d}.png
    ls {a,b,c,d}.png.md        # notes, stories or info about each image
    hee deploy blog \-to lab    # warn on a title\-only post, but deploy it for testing

  into a real post on the resume checkout at \[ga]\-resume\[ga] (default
  \[ga]\[ti]/git/resume\[ga]): a branch \[ga]blog/<oper>\-<slug>\[ga] off \[ga]origin/main\[ga],
  \[ga]profiles/<oper>/blog/<slug>.md\[ga] plus its images copied beside it, built
  with \[ga]./convert.sh\[ga], pushed to lab with \[ga]media/bin/deploy.sh <oper> lab\[ga],
  and a PR that records what is already live. DIR defaults to \[ga].\[ga].

  \[ga]hee deploy store\[ga] turns a store directory (a catalog: a store.yaml, one
  inventory asset + stock record per item, one image and note per item)
  into the live store on the lab: \[ga]rsync \-rlt \-\-delete \-\-chmod=D2775,F664\[ga] the directory to
  \[ga]$MNTPATH/store/<slug>/\[ga] (the share the store host also mounts), a
  \[ga]POST /api/owner/reload\[ga] to pick up the new dataset, and a \[ga]GET /health\[ga]
  to confirm the service is serving it. DIR defaults to \[ga].\[ga]; the slug
  defaults to DIR\[aq]s basename. \[ga]\-to prod\[ga] (phase 1, same as blog) only
  prints the release procedure. \[ga]\-dry\-run\[ga] runs every gate and shows the
  rsync plan (\[ga]\-\-itemize\-changes \-n\[ga]) without touching the share, running
  the reload, or requiring \[ga]STORE_OWNER_TOKEN\[ga].

  \[ga]hee deploy worker\[ga] ships DIR as a Cloudflare Worker with static assets \-\-
  the same path \[ga]hee url deploy\[ga] and tcos\-www use \-\- and attaches \[ga]\-host\[ga]
  to it if given (Cloudflare creates the DNS record itself). Needs Node >=
  20 and a token in CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN or HEE_CRED_PASS with Workers
  Scripts:Edit, plus DNS:Edit on the host\[aq]s zone for \[ga]\-host\[ga]. Built for
  get.hee.tools: the directory holds \[ga]index.html\[ga] (the installer bytes, so
  \[ga]curl \-fsSL https://get.hee.tools | sh\[ga] works) and \[ga]get\-hee.sh\[ga].
  \[ga]\-dry\-run\[ga] lists what would ship and stops before wrangler.

  DIR is the unit of input for blog:

    blog.md               line 1 \[ga]# Title\[ga] (required); line 2 may be
                           \[ga]**Date:** YYYY\-MM\-DD\[ga]; then prose. Markdown
                           only, no raw HTML.
    *.png *.jpg *.jpeg
    *.gif *.webp           figures, in byte\-order filename sort
    <image>.md             the note for that image (e.g. \[ga]a.png.md\[ga] notes
                           \[ga]a.png\[ga]); its first non\-empty line is the
                           figure\[aq]s alt text, the rest is the caption

  The slug is DIR\[aq]s basename, lowercased; it must match
  \[ga]\[ha][a\-z0\-9][a\-z0\-9\-]*$\[ga] or the tool refuses. The oper is \[ga]\-oper\[ga] if given,
  else \[ga]$USER\[ga] when that is a profile under \[ga]<resume>/profiles/\[ga], else the
  tool refuses and lists the profiles it found \-\- it never guesses a
  person.

  DIR is the unit of input for store (one directory per store; a deployed
  store lives at \[ga]$MNTPATH/store/<slug>/\[ga]):

    store.yaml                                                 the store: name (required), tagline,
                                                                currency, pickup, owner, policy
    inventory/objects/asset/<tsz>__inv\-asset\-<sub>\-<id>.yaml    one per item, \[ga]hee inv add \-\-dataset DIR\[ga]
    inventory/objects/stock/<tsz>__inv\-stock\-<id>.yaml          one per item on offer, naming its asset
    images/<stableid>.<png|jpg|jpeg|gif|webp>                   the item\[aq]s picture, keyed by stableid
    images/<stableid>.<ext>.md                                  its note: first non\-empty line is the
                                                                 alt text, the rest the caption

  An item is the pair (asset, stock); the stableid ties asset, stock and
  image together. An asset with no stock record is not for sale. A stock
  record whose asset is missing is refused, never silently dropped.

  \-oper       which person\[aq]s blog; default: $USER if it is a profile
  \-to         lab|prod, default lab. prod (phase 1) only prints the
              release procedure and does nothing else.
  \-slug       (store only) the store\[aq]s slug; default DIR\[aq]s basename,
              lowercased
  \-url        (store only) the running store\[aq]s base URL; default
              https://store.lab.tcos.us
  \-dry\-run      run every gate, print what would be written (blog: the
                assembled post between \[ga]\-\-\-\-\- post \-\-\-\-\-\[ga] markers and the
                files; store: the rsync plan between \[ga]\-\-\-\-\- rsync \-\-\-\-\-\[ga]
                markers), write nothing, touch nothing, run nothing
  \-no\-pr        (blog only) leave the branch local after deploying to lab,
                no PR
  \-list\-missing (store only) print all items without images/notes instead of
                a summary count
  \-resume       (blog only) path to the resume checkout, default \[ti]/git/resume

GATES for blog (in order, each with its exit code)
  DIR missing, or no blog.md, or line 1 not \[aq]# Title\[aq]    CRITICAL 2, refuse
  slug not slug\-safe                                     CRITICAL 2, refuse
  \-oper not a profile dir with profile.json              CRITICAL 2, refuse, lists profiles
  an <image>.md note whose image is absent               CRITICAL 2, refuse
  blog.md has a title and no other non\-empty line        WARNING 1 on lab (deploys anyway),
                                                          CRITICAL 2 on prod (refuse)
  an image with no note                                  WARNING 1, deploys anyway
  \-to prod                                                UNKNOWN 3, prints the release
                                                          procedure, does nothing

GATES for store (in order, each with its exit code)
  no store.yaml, or store.yaml has no \[aq]name\[aq]             CRITICAL 2, refuse
  slug not slug\-safe                                     CRITICAL 2, refuse
  no asset record, or no stock record                    CRITICAL 2, refuse, names the missing kind
  a stock record whose \[aq]asset\[aq] names no asset in DIR     CRITICAL 2, refuse, names the stock file
  an item (has stock) with no image                      WARNING 1, deploys anyway; one summary
                                                          line per kind, \-list\-missing names each
  an image with no note                                  WARNING 1, deploys anyway; same
  \-to prod                                                UNKNOWN 3, prints the release
                                                          procedure, does nothing
  STORE_OWNER_TOKEN unset (real deploy only, not \-dry\-run)  CRITICAL 2, refuse before rsync,
                                                             names the variable
  $MNTPATH/store not a writable directory                CRITICAL 2, refuse before rsync
  rsync exits non\-zero                                   CRITICAL 2, refuse, nothing reloaded
  the reload\[aq]s \[aq]unloadable\[aq] list is non\-empty            CRITICAL 2, printed one per line
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.IP
.EX
  0  OK \-\- deployed (or dry\-run completed) clean
  1  WARNING \-\- deployed (or dry\-run completed) anyway
  2  CRITICAL \-\- refused; nothing written, nothing deployed
  3  UNKNOWN \-\- \-to prod: printed the release procedure, did nothing else

NOT IN V1
  media and meme kinds, \-to prod beyond printing the procedure, editing an
  existing blog post or store item, deleting images, more than one store
  per service instance, notifications, payment.
.EE
